PTForge
=======

PTForge is a JavaScript scripting extension for Cisco Packet Tracer. It adds
an editor, a terminal and a debugger to Packet Tracer, and a library of more
than 380 functions for building topologies, configuring Cisco IOS devices,
servers and hosts, and verifying the result.

A script can place devices, cable them, configure VLANs, routing, security
and server services, and then test reachability across the whole network.
The editor works like Visual Studio Code, with tabs, IntelliSense, a
JavaScript terminal that runs inside Packet Tracer and a step debugger.
Plugins in .pf files can add commands, functions and lab checks.

WARNING: PTForge is in early development and still contains known bugs.
Several features have only been tested outside Packet Tracer. Check the
results of your scripts and keep backups of your .pkt files.

Quick Start
-----------

* Get the latest release: https://github.com/r4chan842/PTForge/releases/latest
* Install it: https://r4chan842.github.io/PTForge/guides/installation.html
* Write a first script: https://r4chan842.github.io/PTForge/guides/getting-started.html
* Report a bug: https://github.com/r4chan842/PTForge/issues

Essential Documentation
-----------------------

All users should be familiar with:

* Requirements and installation: https://r4chan842.github.io/PTForge/guides/installation.html
* Known limitations: https://r4chan842.github.io/PTForge/guides/limitations.html
* Function reference: https://r4chan842.github.io/PTForge/api/index.html
* Cisco Packet Tracer API: https://tutorials.ptnetacad.net/help/default/IpcAPI/annotated.html

The complete documentation, including translations, can be viewed online at:
https://r4chan842.github.io/PTForge/


Who Are You?
============

Find your role below:

* Student: Building and checking CCNA labs
* Instructor: Preparing labs and grading them
* Network Engineer: Automating topologies and configurations
* Plugin Author: Extending PTForge with .pf plugins
* Contributor: Working on PTForge itself


